<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>STSDG-based Generation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we evaluate every key stage in Spatial-Temporal Semantic Dependency Graph Construction.
We use the human evaluation
to verify the reliability in each intermediate stage.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Are the generated questions reliable?</span>
The first stage of our evaluation framework is to extract all facts and then transform them into a question format.
Therefore, it is very important to get high-quality questions.
To evaluate the quality of the generated questions, we define the metrics precision and recall. For each text, we employ annotators to write the corresponding facts, denoted as <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{c_{1},\cdots,c_{n_{c}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{c_{1},\cdots,c_{n_{c}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Follow the definition of the last section, the generated questions are denoted as <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\{q_{1},\cdots,q_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\{q_{1},\cdots,q_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the generated questions and annotated facts, we define <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum m_{t,q}/|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum m_{t,q}/|Q|</annotation></semantics></math> as precision and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum m_{t,q}/|T|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum m_{t,q}/|T|</annotation></semantics></math> as recall. <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|</annotation></semantics></math> are the total number of questions and facts, respectively. <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t,q}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t,q}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise, it is <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. We show the experimental results in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 STSDG-based Generation ‣ 4 Meta Evaluation for FIFA ‣ FIFA: Unified Faithfulness Evaluation Framework for Text-to-Video and Video-to-Text Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Overall, the generated questions are close to perfect in matching the source semantic fact.
Furthermore, we compute the consistency between 3 annotators and found Fleiss’ Kappa is 0.84, which indicates an almost perfect agreement between annotators.</p>
</div>
